The timestamp was authenticated by a TSA whose configured validity period ended
before the timestamp. An unrelated TSA entry has no certificates but has a
validity period covering the timestamp. Verification must fail: temporal
authorization must come from the TSA that authenticated the timestamp.

Creation: copy the bundle and trusted root from
`rekor2-timestamp-outside-trust-root-tsa-validity_fail`, then append an unrelated
TSA with an empty certificate chain and validity from `2025-06-01T00:00:00Z` to
`2025-07-01T00:00:00Z`, which covers the bundle's timestamp.
